===Etymology===
From {{inh|fr|frm|hyver}}, from {{inh|fr|fro|hyveir}}, {{m|fro|yver}}, {{m|fro|iver}}, from {{der|fr|la|hībernum}} [''tempus''] (a borrowing, according to the Trésor de la Langue Française, and first documented in 1282), whence also [[Italian]] {{m|it|inverno}} and Spanish {{m|es|invierno}}. Close related to [[Catalan]] {{m|ca|hivern}}. Ultimately from {{der|fr|ine-pro||*ǵʰey-m-r-ino-}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*ǵʰey-}}

